                <pb facs="0723" n="623" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg623"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/7660: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-11-11T18:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 11,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 12—3:21
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>569. Reference McCully’s 88 of November 10th, 4 p.m. This dispatch evidently
                    refers to authority for High Commission to furnish aid with funds, because every
                    possible aid is being given Admiral McCully, likewise all American interests in
                    Crimea, by using naval vessels and every other means I legally can employ.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
